@copilot Update this PR directly with one metadata-only completion of its new duration-metric support. Preserve the main base, draft state, all current runtime code and tests, RPC preview gating, legacy-only absence, and existing description explaining that metrics require preview. Do not create another PR or edit its title or description.

instrumentation/spring/spring-rmi-4.0/metadata.yaml now describes duration metrics but its semantic_conventions list still declares only RPC_CLIENT_SPANS and RPC_SERVER_SPANS. Add RPC_CLIENT_METRICS and RPC_SERVER_METRICS alongside their corresponding span entries, following instrumentation/rmi/metadata.yaml in PR #20992 and other RPC metric instrumentations. Copilot review 5659804489 has no findings; the code and coverage have been verified, but the supported-signal inventory still needs this directly related update.

Make only the missing metadata declarations. Do not refactor production code, rewrite metric assertions, change unknown-method handling, or touch native Java RMI. Use any existing narrow metadata formatting/validation command if applicable; do not introduce tooling, run broad builds, disable caches, or edit unrelated files.

